{:edb/db-before-t 862 :edb/db-after-t 863 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534175 50 #inst "2026-10-06T07:37:30.731Z" 13194139534175 true] [17592186114838 1100 "Is the function $y=f(x)$, plotted below, differentiable at $x=-1$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/b9be6cb7e47a4541bf7daca4184816a7.png)" 13194139534175 false] [17592186114838 1100 "Is the function $y=f(x),$ plotted below, differentiable at $x=-1?$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/assets/fafd2847f21de3f9f35e05dac61e8a5e406ede40ef7fba014ca5c01eb6d6cdd6.png)" 13194139534175 true] [17592186114838 1145 "The function $y=f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=-1$.\n\nThe function has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1$. Since it is not continuous at $x=-1$, it is also not differentiable there." 13194139534175 false] [17592186114838 1145 "The function $y=f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=-1.$\n\nThe function has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$ Since it is not continuous at $x=-1,$ it is also not differentiable there." 13194139534175 true] [17592186114839 1100 "Which of the following functions are differentiable at the point $x=-1$?\n\n- $f(x) = x^5+1$\n- $g(x) = \\dfrac{2}{x+1}$" 13194139534175 false] [17592186114839 1100 "Which of the following functions are differentiable at the point $x=-1?$\n\n- $f(x) = x^5+1$\n\n- $g(x) = \\dfrac{2}{x+1}$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186114839 1145 "Let's analyze each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is a polynomial and is therefore differentiable and continuous for all $x$.\n- The function $g(x)$ has an essential discontinuity at $x=-1$, so it is not differentiable at $x=-1$ either.\n\nIn conclusion, only $f(x)$ is differentiable at the point $x=-1$." 13194139534175 false] [17592186114839 1145 "Let's analyze each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is a polynomial and is therefore differentiable and continuous for all $x.$\n\n- The function $g(x)$ has an essential discontinuity at $x=-1,$ so it is not differentiable at $x=-1$ either.\n\nIn conclusion, only $f(x)$ is differentiable at the point $x=-1.$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186114840 1100 "Consider the function $y = f(x)$ whose graph is plotted below. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/assets/59499238b529d4d583885cf2c06bae11991c7d3fb5f84f347158e774e2b4ae00.png)" 13194139534175 true] [17592186114840 1100 "Consider the function $y = f(x)$ whose graph is plotted below. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/e2fa4c174a5001cf56d29ee8a17509dd.png)" 13194139534175 false] [17592186114840 1145 "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a vertical tangent, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=1$ the function has a cusp, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=2$ the function has a removable discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=0, 1, 2.$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186114840 1145 "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a vertical tangent, so it's not differentiable there.\n- At $x=1$ the function has a cusp, so it's not differentiable there.\n- At $x=2$ the function has a removable discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=0, 1, 2$." 13194139534175 false] [17592186115300 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280475 13194139534175 true] [17592186115300 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280482 13194139534175 true] [17592186115300 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280538 13194139534175 true] [17592186115300 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280545 13194139534175 true] [17592186115300 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280552 13194139534175 true] [17592186115301 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280503 13194139534175 true] [17592186115301 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280517 13194139534175 true] [17592186115301 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280524 13194139534175 true] [17592186115301 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280559 13194139534175 true] [17592186115301 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280566 13194139534175 true] [17592186115302 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280489 13194139534175 true] [17592186115302 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280496 13194139534175 true] [17592186115302 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280510 13194139534175 true] [17592186115302 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280531 13194139534175 true] [17592186115796 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534175 true] [17592186115796 1100 "Which of the following functions is not differentiable over the entire interval $x ∈ (-1, 1)$ due to the existence of a vertical tangent in the interval?" 13194139534175 false] [17592186115796 1100 "Which of the following functions is not differentiable over the entire interval $x\\in (-1,1)$ due to the existence of a vertical tangent in the interval?" 13194139534175 true] [17592186115796 1145 "Notice that the function $y=h(x)$ has a vertical tangent at $x=0$ and is therefore not differentiable at $x=0.$ \nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=h(x).$\n\nThe other graphs do not have a vertical tangent inside the interval $(-1,1).$\n\n- The function $y=f(x)$ has a corner point at $x=0.$\n\n- The function $y=g(x)$ is smooth and continuous over the entire interval $x\\in (-1,1).$\n\n- The functions $y=p(x)$ and $y=q(x)$ are not defined at $x=0.$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280475 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280476 13194139534175 true] [17592186280475 1089 "q-101964" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280475 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534175 true] [17592186280475 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/assets/80fca5dc871cd083e638472abaf26b2a8ba91e81cfa5372df7398b4b63346dfa.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is continuous at $x=5$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=10$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280475 1113 #uuid "7751155c-8e19-5510-944b-ebee6e554dd2" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280475 1145 "- Statement I is true. The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=0$ without taking a pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=5$ without taking a pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the function is not continuous at $x=10$, it can't be differentiable at that point.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280477 13194139534175 true] [17592186280476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280478 13194139534175 true] [17592186280476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280479 13194139534175 true] [17592186280476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280480 13194139534175 true] [17592186280476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280481 13194139534175 true] [17592186280476 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280476 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280476 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280480 13194139534175 true] [17592186280476 1110 #uuid "17c89265-c5ce-54dd-a27f-42467b37d23d" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280477 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280477 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280477 1111 #uuid "26960bd6-f746-5870-bf1d-69df993a2580" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280478 1034 "I only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280478 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280478 1111 #uuid "2594edf5-c303-55e2-af84-7432f5ec8a02" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280479 1034 "III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280479 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280479 1111 #uuid "0f30437e-e83d-53b4-8704-d1ad464b3353" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280480 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280480 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280480 1111 #uuid "d5b8b880-5515-5873-9384-4788d5611d34" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280481 1034 "II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280481 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280481 1111 #uuid "801fe666-f32c-58e0-9865-319e160f96c2" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280482 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280483 13194139534175 true] [17592186280482 1089 "q-101983" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280482 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534175 true] [17592186280482 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/assets/dc27a54ac20efc84bfbc404a20a91309c60c3fb42118f164129e93eee584437b.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=-5$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=-5$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=0$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280482 1113 #uuid "71b1d824-b07f-58a9-9408-c51993cdaaec" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280482 1145 "- Statement I is false. The function has an infinite discontinuity at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-5$ it can't be differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is continuous at $x=0$ and doesn't have a corner point, a  cusp, or a vertical tangent.\n\nTherefore, only statement III  is true." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280484 13194139534175 true] [17592186280483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280485 13194139534175 true] [17592186280483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280486 13194139534175 true] [17592186280483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280487 13194139534175 true] [17592186280483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280488 13194139534175 true] [17592186280483 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280483 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280483 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280485 13194139534175 true] [17592186280483 1110 #uuid "5ebc2692-9d63-50d4-a12f-bee802e69f6c" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280484 1034 "I only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280484 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280484 1111 #uuid "f518edbf-834f-5243-acb7-b41a1a911e78" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280485 1034 "III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280485 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280485 1111 #uuid "c73c7f8f-9f0a-5561-9525-a7954c4cb58a" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280486 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280486 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280486 1111 #uuid "5bedc3c0-cb9a-5761-9cb4-aaae6d2f0d4e" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280487 1034 "None of the statements" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280487 1111 #uuid "7cbc3fe1-8ec0-5c3f-ae5c-702cb7310778" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280488 1034 "II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280488 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280488 1111 #uuid "78c12121-cb3b-5692-a3e9-e27152d4e6e4" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280489 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280490 13194139534175 true] [17592186280489 1089 "q-101994" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280489 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534175 true] [17592186280489 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/assets/ce2ec4b51b4c55975bf25234fdfbfa98663ae95ef7ee2bd5a774c4e4d4655292.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280489 1113 #uuid "002228be-6172-506e-9310-e16f6f583b31" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280489 1145 "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a cusp, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=1$ the function has a jump discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is  $x=0$ and $x=1.$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280491 13194139534175 true] [17592186280490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280492 13194139534175 true] [17592186280490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280493 13194139534175 true] [17592186280490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280494 13194139534175 true] [17592186280490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280495 13194139534175 true] [17592186280490 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280490 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280490 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280493 13194139534175 true] [17592186280490 1110 #uuid "0edc67ed-8886-5543-a970-59a15eaee2d8" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280491 1034 "$x=0$ only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280491 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280491 1111 #uuid "4c66f89c-c9df-53cc-8bc8-210bc95e27ea" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280492 1034 "$x=1$ only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280492 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280492 1111 #uuid "b83ce08e-e786-5d04-be3e-2d240cd4c322" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280493 1034 "$x=0$ and $x=1$ only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280493 1111 #uuid "d4fa0f86-6d26-5c87-bf26-594329bed878" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280494 1034 "$x=-1$ only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280494 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280494 1111 #uuid "6a7406a5-9526-5a34-a50f-21d937be781d" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280495 1034 "$x=-1,$ $x=0,$ and $x=1$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280495 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280495 1111 #uuid "e3e67f65-9319-5c95-b077-eb490494aa98" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280496 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280497 13194139534175 true] [17592186280496 1089 "q-101995" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280496 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534175 true] [17592186280496 1100 "Given that a function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$, has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$, and is differentiable at $x=-1$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\n- It is differentiable at $x=0$\n- It  is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n- It is continuous at $x=-1$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280496 1113 #uuid "0bec816a-4724-5c20-95e7-b52e7d3f32fc" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280496 1145 "- Statement I is false. Continuity does not imply differentiability. For example, the function $y=|x|$ is continuous but it's not differentiable at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true.  A function that is discontinuous at a point can't be differentiable at this point (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, differentiability implies continuity." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280498 13194139534175 true] [17592186280497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280499 13194139534175 true] [17592186280497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280500 13194139534175 true] [17592186280497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280501 13194139534175 true] [17592186280497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280502 13194139534175 true] [17592186280497 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280497 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280497 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280498 13194139534175 true] [17592186280497 1110 #uuid "94656019-44ee-53c5-8da1-18fbcb22b7e0" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280498 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280498 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280498 1111 #uuid "8ff78273-1b14-5ddf-8000-b7b5ce47a464" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280499 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280499 1111 #uuid "23f8b208-73c1-5119-aee4-9ad695409c2f" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280500 1034 "III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280500 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280500 1111 #uuid "5a0988c3-4db4-59ab-bdcc-694e11c5f6bd" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280501 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280501 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280501 1111 #uuid "d393ac36-bd23-54ba-ae5f-06d6e9ccf259" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280502 1034 "II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280502 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280502 1111 #uuid "2a2e917c-5b8b-58e8-b018-2127b0763ac0" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280503 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280504 13194139534175 true] [17592186280503 1089 "q-102159" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280503 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534175 true] [17592186280503 1100 "Which of the following functions is differentiable at the point $x=-1?$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280503 1113 #uuid "46edc91d-e7f5-50a1-b76e-fb0eba0a8481" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280503 1145 "Notice that the function $h(x)$ is differentiable for all $x\\ne 1.$ Therefore, the correct answer is $h(x)=\\frac{1}{x-1}.$\n\nThe other functions are not differentiable at $x=-1.$\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=-1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $p(x)$ has a vertical tangent at $x=-1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $q(x)$ has a corner point at $x=-1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $g(x)$ is not defined at $x=-1$ and hence it is not differentiable there." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280505 13194139534175 true] [17592186280504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280506 13194139534175 true] [17592186280504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280507 13194139534175 true] [17592186280504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280508 13194139534175 true] [17592186280504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280509 13194139534175 true] [17592186280504 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280504 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280504 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280508 13194139534175 true] [17592186280504 1110 #uuid "8b5d3f4a-4c41-569b-bdf4-aa84204fa7f7" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280505 1034 "q(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x,\\, & x<-1 \\\\ x-1,\\, & x\\ge -1\\end{aligned}" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280505 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280505 1111 #uuid "a9ed2876-9c70-5df1-bea3-28a1d84eda17" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280506 1034 "g(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280506 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280506 1111 #uuid "18477b97-c937-5785-977f-8313442363c7" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280507 1034 "f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-1}" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280507 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280507 1111 #uuid "a054dab7-6cfb-5117-9710-009355c0a7b8" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280508 1034 "h(x)=\\frac{1}{x-1}" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280508 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280508 1111 #uuid "bcb3904f-ab57-574e-95ba-587ffbff42a2" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280509 1034 "p(x)=\\sqrt[5]{x+1}" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280509 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280509 1111 #uuid "f2845557-be1e-5715-a89d-8f255fcd1de1" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280510 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280511 13194139534175 true] [17592186280510 1089 "q-47670" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280510 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534175 true] [17592186280510 1100 "Given that a function $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=1$, is differentiable at $x=2$, and has a vertical asymptote at $x=3$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\n- It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n- It  is continuous at $x=2$\n- It is differentiable at $x=3$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280510 1113 #uuid "46865db0-9da2-58cc-8805-6fc82c34bf99" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280510 1145 "Differentiability implies continuity. Hence,\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$, it can't be differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement II is true.   Since $f(x)$ is differentiable at $x=2$ it is also  continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since we have a vertical asymptote at $x=3$, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous at this point, hence it can't be differentiable at $x=3$ either." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280512 13194139534175 true] [17592186280511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280513 13194139534175 true] [17592186280511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280514 13194139534175 true] [17592186280511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280515 13194139534175 true] [17592186280511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280516 13194139534175 true] [17592186280511 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280511 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280511 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280516 13194139534175 true] [17592186280511 1110 #uuid "2e597486-4f3d-5e3d-81fc-c87f5c6f2322" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280512 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280512 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280512 1111 #uuid "e339c004-6f98-5b1a-b6d1-9cb41801eb23" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280513 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280513 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280513 1111 #uuid "937ff6de-4be2-5339-a241-5d22bb7202d6" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280514 1034 "I only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280514 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280514 1111 #uuid "292b4aaf-e572-535c-b1ec-2ff65c941c3f" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280515 1034 "III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280515 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280515 1111 #uuid "c88d96ff-7cc7-5c11-a4c7-ccd3c6a0b983" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280516 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280516 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280516 1111 #uuid "541a4392-08cc-5e82-8c3d-59b4531a9115" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280517 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280518 13194139534175 true] [17592186280517 1089 "q-47680" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280517 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534175 true] [17592186280517 1100 "Which of the following functions is differentiable at the point $x=-2?$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280517 1113 #uuid "7d0eb31e-00b8-5cab-baf1-ea4a71c1aca7" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280517 1145 "Notice that the function $p(x)$ is differentiable for all real number $x.$ Therefore, the correct answer is $p(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nAll other functions are not differentiable at $x=-2.$\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=-2$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $g(x)$ has a corner point at $x=-2$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $h(x)$has a vertical tangent at $x=-2$, and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $q(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=-2$ and hence it is not differentiable there." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280518 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280519 13194139534175 true] [17592186280518 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280520 13194139534175 true] [17592186280518 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280521 13194139534175 true] [17592186280518 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280522 13194139534175 true] [17592186280518 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280523 13194139534175 true] [17592186280518 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280518 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280518 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280523 13194139534175 true] [17592186280518 1110 #uuid "453aab19-db93-56bf-bd0d-77c5046deb7f" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280519 1034 "h(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x+2}" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280519 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280519 1111 #uuid "140e4e13-b1ff-5cbb-b34b-6f86109cc2a3" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280520 1034 "f(x)=\\frac{x}{x+2}" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280520 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280520 1111 #uuid "bd58eda1-413f-5637-8d17-0bbb88b3f8c5" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280521 1034 "g(x)=2|x+2|" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280521 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280521 1111 #uuid "3f36fdd6-c55a-5179-8a26-414408ac7d34" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280522 1034 "q(x)={\\begin{aligned}x,\\, & x<-2 \\\\ x-2,\\, & x\\ge -2\\end{aligned}" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280522 1111 #uuid "36ed0c88-6717-5b68-a863-82a514be1196" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280523 1034 "p(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280523 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534175 true] [17592186280523 1111 #uuid "b73f7d30-ca81-5401-b313-fccb31b50d2b" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280524 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280525 13194139534175 true] [17592186280524 1089 "q-47681" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280524 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534175 true] [17592186280524 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+1, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ 3, & x=1\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\n- It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n- It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n- It is differentiable on the interval $(-1,2)$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280524 1113 #uuid "f0ff0842-96b0-56ec-a561-8c9fa764c1ca" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280524 1145 "Let's analyze each statement individually. \n\n- Statement I is false.  At $x=1$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}({x}^{3}+1)={1}^{3}+1=2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}({x}^{3}+1)={1}^{3}+1=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)\\ne f(1)=3,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$ ($f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$).\n\n- Statement II is true. Since  $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1,$ it is also not differentiable there (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=1,$ it is not differentiable on any interval containing this point. Consequently, it is not differentiable on $(-1,2).$\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280526 13194139534175 true] [17592186280525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280527 13194139534175 true] [17592186280525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280528 13194139534175 true] [17592186280525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280529 13194139534175 true] [17592186280525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280530 13194139534175 true] [17592186280525 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280525 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280525 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280530 13194139534175 true] [17592186280525 1110 #uuid "b9c7b53b-b0d7-5232-a529-b0fbb684c697" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280526 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280526 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280526 1111 #uuid "b00ef24b-b0fa-5085-ae3a-db8fea58916d" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280527 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280527 1111 #uuid "b75398cb-dcef-57d8-a605-625b7e970d42" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280528 1034 "III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280528 1111 #uuid "c24e39f8-84e1-5a75-bf0e-4a9ffd7fa725" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280529 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280529 1111 #uuid "536cfb33-9ec5-5e57-9014-9be7d8a50778" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280530 1034 "II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280530 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280530 1111 #uuid "ae34c201-b60c-5ae3-8ebf-150bc26bd7d0" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280531 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280532 13194139534175 true] [17592186280531 1089 "q-47685" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280531 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534175 true] [17592186280531 1100 "Which of the following functions is not differentiable over the entire interval $x\\in (-1,1)$ due to the existence of a cusp?" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280531 1113 #uuid "0ccce8a3-bf9d-5a78-aab6-47b5f04c990b" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280531 1145 "The function $y=q(x)$ has a cusp at $x=0$ and is therefore not differentiable at $x=0.$ So $y=q(x)$ is the correct answer.\n\nThe other graphs do not have a cusp within the interval $(-1,1).$\n\n- The function $y=f(x)$ has a vertical tangent at $x=0$ and is therefore not differentiable at $x=0.$\n\n- The function $y=g(x)$ is smooth and continuous over the entire interval $x\\in (-1,1)$ and is therefore differentiable at every point in the interval.\n\n- The function $y=p(x)$ is not defined at $x=0$ and is therefore not differentiable at $x=0.$\n\n- The function $y=h(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=0$ and is therefore not differentiable at $x=0.$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280533 13194139534175 true] [17592186280532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280534 13194139534175 true] [17592186280532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280535 13194139534175 true] [17592186280532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280536 13194139534175 true] [17592186280532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280537 13194139534175 true] [17592186280532 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280532 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280532 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280536 13194139534175 true] [17592186280532 1110 #uuid "06dc3fca-67f9-525f-bdf8-76259e6db818" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280533 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980056/assets/ba2e2109b1cbf4271cc034f55a51382eab026e8316da4618a5479a24eef0ba43.png" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534175 true] [17592186280533 1111 #uuid "15