iable there.\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=2$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III  are true." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280554 13194139534175 true] [17592186280553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280555 13194139534175 true] [17592186280553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280556 13194139534175 true] [17592186280553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280557 13194139534175 true] [17592186280553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280558 13194139534175 true] [17592186280553 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280553 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280553 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280554 13194139534175 true] [17592186280553 1110 #uuid "7a86a6f7-327b-5b40-9833-09d09f653150" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280554 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280554 1111 #uuid "67540de9-55ee-5afe-8643-f637b91364b4" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280555 1034 "I only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280555 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280555 1111 #uuid "c1e913d7-323b-54cd-aaed-48a78b335904" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280556 1034 "III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280556 1111 #uuid "4047646c-a17f-5165-9c91-a3958a3c0cca" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280557 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280557 1111 #uuid "1ab6056c-76ee-53f7-b25f-ae08303549a1" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280558 1034 "II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280558 1111 #uuid "56f81cd6-629c-57e8-ad3f-5bcb408fce0c" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280559 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280560 13194139534175 true] [17592186280559 1089 "q-73267" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280559 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534175 true] [17592186280559 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-1, & x\\ne 0 \\\\ 1, & x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- It is continuous and differentiable at $x=0$\n- It is **not** continuous at $x=0$ but it is differentiable at $x=0$\n- It is **not** differentiable on the interval $x\\in (-1,1)$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280559 1113 #uuid "68d793ec-aaf3-5b37-877d-af06a0a967e4" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280559 1145 "Let's analyze each statement individually.\n\n- Statement I is false. First, we investigate the continuity of $f(x)$ . It is continuous everywhere except, possibly, $x=0.$ At this point, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}({x}^{3}-1)={0}^{3}-1=-1 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}({x}^{3}-1)={0}^{3}-1=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)\\ne f(0)=1,\n$$\n\n \nand so $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0.$ Therefore, it's not differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0,$ it is also not differentiable there.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=0,$ it is not differentiable on any interval that includes this point. Consequently, it is not differentiable in $x\\in (-1,1).$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280561 13194139534175 true] [17592186280560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280562 13194139534175 true] [17592186280560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280563 13194139534175 true] [17592186280560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280564 13194139534175 true] [17592186280560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280565 13194139534175 true] [17592186280560 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280560 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280560 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280563 13194139534175 true] [17592186280560 1110 #uuid "4e1287e4-30db-5043-afeb-beaf61b74880" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280561 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280561 1111 #uuid "19881840-23cb-5bd9-af51-c86a13510dfe" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280562 1034 "I only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280562 1111 #uuid "52d638f2-0a10-50f1-9c4a-defa261ce77c" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280563 1034 "III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280563 1111 #uuid "8b1d8d21-9a86-5967-ac82-24017082b5f8" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280564 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280564 1111 #uuid "cdf8a5e6-9613-5a14-844b-a46eb9ce6338" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280565 1034 "II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280565 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280565 1111 #uuid "5bd0f9c3-2d18-57a4-92b9-691a28014f86" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280566 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280567 13194139534175 true] [17592186280566 1089 "q-73270" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280566 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534175 true] [17592186280566 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+1, & x<1 \\\\ 2, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\n- It is continuous at $x=1$\n- It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n- It is differentiable on the interval $(0,2)$" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280566 1113 #uuid "9d3d55e7-45c3-56ac-8489-9d0883fda9fa" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280566 1145 "- Statement I and II are true. Indeed, let's investigate the continuity of $f(x).$ It is continuous everywhere except, possibly at  $x=1.$ At this point, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}(x+1)=1+1=2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}2=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)=f(1)=2,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is  continuous at $x=1$ . However, $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=1$ because it has a corner point there: \n\n$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)=1\\,$  if  $\\,x<1$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0\\,$ if $\\,x>1$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=1,$ it is not differentiable on any interval containing this point. Consequently, it is not differentiable on $(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534175 true] [17592186280567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280568 13194139534175 true] [17592186280567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280569 13194139534175 true] [17592186280567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280570 13194139534175 true] [17592186280567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280571 13194139534175 true] [17592186280567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280572 13194139534175 true] [17592186280567 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534175 true] [17592186280567 1041 "selection" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280567 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280571 13194139534175 true] [17592186280567 1110 #uuid "86d977f7-1583-58e8-898d-6a3d5a2b8050" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280568 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280568 1111 #uuid "9408aea0-188c-576f-9cbc-30b4f7d7dcb1" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280569 1034 "I only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280569 1111 #uuid "bdbfa959-c4b3-57a8-8635-ab5704290f17" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280570 1034 "III only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280570 1111 #uuid "3a4a061c-1dce-539c-bb12-aaa3ed87a30f" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280571 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534175 true] [17592186280571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534175 true] [17592186280571 1111 #uuid "b971f998-7ede-5e2a-99